# File: stdlib/patches/0002-remove-fixity-declarations-for-closed-operators.patch
#
# What: agda/agda-stdlib commit 1b7f26af455caa57e9372cef50b4f4118a92bf81
# (branch agda-master, Andreas Abel, 2026-09-08), cherry-picked onto v2.3
# without change: fixity declarations for closed operators removed, which
# Agda 2.9.0 warns about.
#
# Why: the standard library 2.3, which agda-algebras depends on, checks
# whole under Agda 2.9.0 (all 1,154 modules) with these five patches and
# with no released version (issue 61: row 2b, and two later fixes); the
# page ships it so patched (issue 58).
#
# Against: agda/agda-stdlib v2.3 (8326c7475af1fa456ca04a0203c168d5d7ff842b),
# applied in order by the flake (packages.stdlib).
#
From 1d7e2dae49e88e32f24b6ff9f714028dc26c63e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Abel <andreas.abel@ifi.lmu.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:11:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Remove fixity declarations for closed operators

Addresses these two issues:
1. A non-operator `Agda.Builtin.Int.pos` is imported as prefix operator `+_` without giving it an explicit fixity declaration.
2. Some non-operators are given a fixity where it does not make sense.

Both issues are just of cosmetic nature atm, but may change to become issues in the future, see agda/agda#1438 .

It seems best to address these issues now.
Note that the syntax addressing issue 1 has been available since Agda 2.6.1 already.

Closes #3114.
---
 src/Data/Integer/Base.agda                      |  5 ++---
 src/Data/Refinement/Base.agda                   |  1 -
 src/Data/Vec/Relation/Binary/Equality/Cast.agda |  2 +-
 src/Relation/Binary/Reasoning/Syntax.agda       | 11 +++++------
 src/Relation/Nary.agda                          |  2 --
 src/Relation/Unary.agda                         |  2 --
 src/Text/Regex/Base.agda                        |  3 +--
 7 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Data/Integer/Base.agda b/src/Data/Integer/Base.agda
index 9d7e689db..15d2cdfb2 100644
--- a/src/Data/Integer/Base.agda
+++ b/src/Data/Integer/Base.agda
@@ -37,8 +37,8 @@ open import Agda.Builtin.Int public
   using ()
   renaming
   ( Int    to ℤ
-  ; pos    to +_      -- "+ n"      stands for "n"
-  ; negsuc to -[1+_]  -- "-[1+ n ]" stands for "- (1 + n)"
+  ; pos    to infix 8 +_  -- "+ n"      stands for "n"
+  ; negsuc to -[1+_]      -- "-[1+ n ]" stands for "- (1 + n)"
   )
 
 -- Some additional patterns that provide symmetry around 0
@@ -345,4 +345,3 @@ i % j = i %ℕ ∣ j ∣
   ; 0# = 0ℤ
   ; 1# = 1ℤ
   }
-
diff --git a/src/Data/Refinement/Base.agda b/src/Data/Refinement/Base.agda
